  <data key="d5">Cubist-like designs are created by Louis Barrilet in the stained-glass windows of the American bar at the Atrium Casino in Dax (1926), but also including names of fashionable cocktails.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:pierre chareau" target="Movement:the french union of modern artists" id="BELONGS_TO|70">
  <data key="d3">BELONGS_TO</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Art_Deco.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Its members included architects Pierre Chareau, Francis Jourdain, Robert Mallet-Stevens, Le Corbusier, and, in the Soviet Union, Konstantin Melnikov; the Irish designer Eileen Gray; the French designer Sonia Delaunay; and the jewellers Georges Fouquet and Jean Puiforcat.</data>
</edge>
