</edge>
<edge source="Person:jules leleu" target="Work:furniture for the dining room of the élysée palace" id="DESIGNED|99">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Art_Deco.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Jules Leleu was a traditional furniture designer who moved smoothly into Art Deco in the 1920s; he designed the furniture for the dining room of the Élysée Palace, and for the first-class cabins of the steamship Normandie.</data>
</edge>
