<edge source="Person:otto wagner" target="Work:austrian postal savings bank" id="DESIGNED|837">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modern_architecture.md</data>
  <data key="d5">He designed a stylized ornamental metro station at Karlsplatz in Vienna (1888–89), then an ornamental Art Nouveau residence, Majolika House (1898), before moving to a much more geometric and simplified style, without ornament, in the Austrian Postal Savings Bank (1904–1906).</data>
</edge>
