<edge source="Person:adolf loos" target="Work:villa müller" id="DESIGNED|500">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Functionalism_(architecture).md</data>
  <data key="d5">The former Czechoslovakia was an early adopter of the functionalist style, with notable examples such as Villa Tugendhat in Brno, designed by Mies van der Rohe in 1928, Villa Müller in Prague, designed by Adolf Loos in 1930, and the majority of the city of Zlín, developed by the Bata shoe company as a factory town in the 1920s and designed by Le Corbusier's student František Lydie Gahura.</data>
</edge>
