  <data key="d5">In Vitra Conference Pavilion, Weil am Rhein, 1993, the concepts are to bring together the relationships between building, human movement, site, and nature, which as one main point of minimalism ideology establishes dialogue between the building and site.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:kazuyo sejima" target="Work:new museum" id="DESIGNED|826">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Minimalism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Works include New Museum (2010) New York City, Small House (2000) Tokyo, and House surrounded By Plum Trees (2003) Tokyo.</data>
</edge>
