  <data key="d3">STUDIED_AT</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modern_architecture.md</data>
  <data key="d5">In the late 1930s, he moved to the Harvard Graduate School of Design, where he studied with Walter Gropius and Marcel Breuer and became deeply involved in Modernism.</data>
</edge>
