</edge>
<edge source="Person:henry moore" target="Work:nuclear energy" id="DESIGNED|995">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modernism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">On the campus of the University of Chicago in December 1967, 25 years to the minute after the team of physicists led by Enrico Fermi achieved the first controlled, self-sustaining nuclear chain reaction, Moore's Nuclear Energy was unveiled.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:henry moore" target="Work:man enters the cosmos" id="DESIGNED|996">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modernism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Also in Chicago, Moore commemorated science with a large bronze sundial, locally named Man Enters the Cosmos (1980), which was commissioned to recognize the space exploration program.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:eduardo paolozzi" target="Work:i was a rich man's plaything" id="DESIGNED|997">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modernism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">The early works of David Hockney and the works of Richard Hamilton and Eduardo Paolozzi (who created the ground-breaking I was a Rich Man's Plaything, 1947) are considered seminal examples in the movement.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:marcel duchamp" target="Work:fountain" id="DESIGNED|998">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modernism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">In choosing "an ordinary article of life" and creating "a new thought for that object", Duchamp invited onlookers to view Fountain as a sculpture.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:robert rauschenberg" target="Work:erased de kooning drawing" id="DESIGNED|999">
  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Modernism.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Duchamp can be seen as a precursor to conceptual art, other famous examples being John Cage's 4′33″, which is four minutes and thirty three seconds of silence, and Rauschenberg's Erased de Kooning Drawing.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:robert rauschenberg" target="Person:marcel duchamp" id="INFLUENCED_BY|1000">
