  <data key="d3">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Paul_Rand.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Rand was largely "self-taught" as a designer, learning about the works of Cassandre and László Moholy-Nagy from European magazines such as Gebrauchsgraphik."</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:paul rand" target="Person:gustav jensen" id="INFLUENCED_BY|1053">
  <data key="d3">INFLUENCED_BY</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Paul_Rand.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Between his class assignments and his work, Rand was able to amass a fairly large portfolio, largely influenced by the German advertising style Sachplakat (object poster) as well as the works of Gustav Jensen.</data>
</edge>
<edge source="Person:paul rand" target="Institution:yale" id="TAUGHT_AT|1054">
  <data key="d3">TAUGHT_AT</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Paul_Rand.md</data>
  <data key="d5">In 1992, Rand resigned his position at Yale in protest of the appointment of postmodern designer Sheila Levrant de Bretteville, and convinced his colleague Armin Hofmann to do the same.</data>
</edge>
