  <data key="d3">DESIGNED</data>
  <data key="d4">en_Paul_Rand.md</data>
  <data key="d5">Dewey is an important source for Rand's underlying sentiment in graphic design; on page one of Rand's groundbreaking Thoughts on Design, the author begins drawing lines from Dewey's philosophy to the need for "functional-aesthetic perfection" in modern art.</data>
</edge>
